Technical Lead Location: Farnborough or Whiteley, with flexibility to work from home dependent on business demands Salary: £61,500 - £78,800 The Role: The Technical Lead has overall responsibility for all engineering activities and leadership of the team, on the workstream that they are assigned by the Chief Engineer. Their responsibility and accountability extends from project start up through to operations and closedown and includes on contract growth. What will I be doing? Delivery and technical assurance of the solution within the quality, cost and schedule constraints;
Achieving acceptance of the solution by the customer
Providing technical leadership and mentorship across the workstream team;
Ensuring that the engineering processes within the project are commensurate with the requirements of the contracted standards and Leidos corporate governance;
Identifying the skills and staff required to deliver the engineering solution;
Defining the engineering practices and resources required to deliver the project and services within the constraints of the company engineering policies;
Lead and manage effective engineering activities across the project;
Preparing project specific technical documentation in collaboration with project discipline SMEs for PDR, CDR, SRR and SPR reviews and other technical sessions as required;
Lead and deliver updates to baseline HLD / LLD documentation as required by the project;
In collaboration with project PMs prepare technical WBS, PBS and resource BoEs against overall solution proposals for change proposals and on contract growth; What does Leidos need from me? The candidate is required to be a technical leader, able to coordinate and direct engineering teams in successful delivery and acceptance of the system. Ability to execute and perform, with direction from the Chief Engineer, and possess significant practical experience and applied knowledge across the following areas: Complex systems integration projects, involving IT systems;
Technical Management of subcontractors;
Systems Engineering and understanding of the principles behind each of the main processes;
Technical Team Management including the planning of work packages, allocation to team members and reporting;
Technical Team Leadership including providing technical direction to team members; In addition to the areas above, you are required to have: Excellent verbal and written communication skills and work well in a team environment;
Ability to clearly articulate and communicate design and technical concepts in written and verbal forms;
Intellectual calibre and confidence to conduct complex discussions with civilian and service customers and suppliers;
Commercial awareness sufficient to support discussions with customers and suppliers; It would be beneficial if you had experience in the following: Public sector and sensitive projects
Background in Software Engineering or IT Systems Integration
Knowledge of Government or MOD organisation, processes and procedures; Clearance Requirements: The successful applicant will be required to hold and maintain UK Security Clearance What we do for you:
At Leidos we are PASSIONATE about customer success, UNITED as a team and INSPIRED to make a difference. We offer meaningful and engaging careers, a collaborative culture, and support for your career goals, all while nurturing a healthy work-life balance. We provide an employment package that attracts, develops and retains only the best in talent. Our reward scheme includes:
• Contributory Pension Scheme
• Private Medical Insurance
• 33 days Annual Leave (including public and privilege holidays)
• Access to Flexible benefits (including life assurance, health schemes, gym memberships, annual buy and sell holidays and a cycle to work scheme) • Flexi-Time Working Commitment to Diversity: We welcome applications from every part of the community and are committed to a truly diverse and inclusive culture. We foster a sense of belonging, welcoming all perspectives and contributions, and providing equal access to opportunities and resources for everyone. If you have a disability or need any reasonable adjustments during the application and selection stages please let us know, and we will respond in a way that best fits your needs. Who We Are: Leidos UK & EUROPE – we work to make the world safer, healthier, and more efficient through technology, engineering and science. Leidos is a growing company delivering innovative technology and solutions focused on safeguarding critical capabilities and transformation in frontline services, our work in the United Kingdom includes addressing some of the most complex problems in defence, healthcare, government, safety and security, and transportation. What Makes Us Different: Purpose: you can use your passion and abilities at Leidos to keep the people you care about safe. We are at the forefront of machine learning, AI, cyber security and solutions. Using your skills in the technology frontline by helping to build a safer world. You can inspire change. Collaboration: having flexibility to do your job is one of our core benefits, enabling you to become part of our extraordinary team. We have been empowering our people to work flexibly for years. Whether you work from home, the office or on customer sites, we will give you the digital tools and the flexibility to work smarter and align your needs and ours. People: Leidos empowers people from every background to be themselves and gives you the tools to learn new skills by enabling growth whilst developing. We believe that extraordinary people need opportunities to grow, to be inspired and to inspire others. At Leidos, we invest in technical academies, career rotations and a career development plans that enhance your future. If you're looking for comfort, keep scrolling. At Leidos, we outthink, outbuild, and outpace the status quo — because the mission demands it. We're not hiring followers. We're recruiting the ones who disrupt, provoke, and refuse to fail. Step 10 is ancient history. We're already at step 30 — and moving faster than anyone else dares. Original Posting: For U.S. Positions: While subject to change based on business needs, Leidos reasonably anticipates that this job requisition will remain open for at least 3 days with an anticipated close date of no earlier than 3 days after the original posting date as listed above. Pay Range:
£61,500.00-£78,800.00 The Leidos pay range for this job level is a general guideline only and not a guarantee of compensation or salary. Additional factors considered in extending an offer include (but are not limited to) responsibilities of the job, education, experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities, as well as internal equity, alignment with market data, applicable bargaining agreement (if any), or other law.

Leidos has an opening for a Waste Management Technician at NASA Glenn Research Center’s Armstrong Test Facility in Sandusky, Ohio. The Waste Management Technician will support the Waste Management and Environmental teams and spill response program. The Waste Management Technician will ensure proper management of hazardous materials, including the completion and review of waste profiles for Resource Conservation and Recovery Act (RCRA) regulated hazardous waste, universal wastes, used oils, and infectious waste; TSCA regulated asbestos-containing materials, and PCBs. Role will include sampling of environmental media for characterization, stormwater management, Underground Storage Tank inspections, spill response, review of property and equipment for hazards prior to disposal, and DOT transportation services. Must be available to work a flexible schedule and be on call. Must be able to pass a Public Trust background investigation. U.S. Citizenship or U.S. Permanent Residence is required due to length of investigation required for non-U.S. persons. Additional support may include: Inspections;
Waste characterizations;
Review and maintenance of shipping and disposal records;
Completion of reports (weekly, monthly and annual);
Property decontamination and remediation;
Coordinating subcontractors and jobs;
Other duties as assigned Required Education and Skills: High school diploma and 5 years of experience required. Degree in chemistry, environmental science, or related field preferred with experience. Ability to work under variable field conditions (weather, insects, and/or limited personnel and vehicle access). Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite - in particular, Microsoft PowerPoint, Word, and Excel - for presentations, reports, and other uses. Strong interpersonal skills and ability to communicate with many personalities, as the position involves interfacing with client and on-site personnel. Ability to work effectively as part of a team.
Ability to perform continuous physical labor, including moving materials up to 50 pounds. Capability to evaluate problems as they arise; situational awareness; and understanding of how your actions could impact your Team’s overall goals and objectives.
Ability to follow prescribed safety procedures at all times while performing various duties. Desired Experience: OSHA 40 hr. HAZWOPER training
Prior experience working with hazardous materials, knowledge of RCRA disposal regulations, knowledge of DOT regulations, knowledge of BUSTR regulations. Experience operating lift equipment, such as forklifts, straight trucks with lift gates, pallet jacks and drum dollies. Preferred Experience: A suitable applicant will be current in the following trainings or will have the ability to obtain the following within the first 90 days of employment. Resource Conservation and Recovery Act (RCRA) training
U.S. Department of Transportation (DOT) training
OSHA 29 CFR Hazardous Waste Operations and Emergency Response (HAZWOPER) 40-hour training
FEMA Incident Command System (ICS) trainings ICS-100, 200, 300, and 700 If you're looking for comfort, keep scrolling. At Leidos, we outthink, outbuild, and outpace the status quo — because the mission demands it. We're not hiring followers. We're recruiting the ones who disrupt, provoke, and refuse to fail. Step 10 is ancient history. We're already at step 30 — and moving faster than anyone else dares. Original Posting:
March 16, 2026 For U.S. Positions: While subject to change based on business needs, Leidos reasonably anticipates that this job requisition will remain open for at least 3 days with an anticipated close date of no earlier than 3 days after the original posting date as listed above. Pay Range:
Pay Range $40,300.00 - $72,850.00 The Leidos pay range for this job level is a general guideline only and not a guarantee of compensation or salary. Additional factors considered in extending an offer include (but are not limited to) responsibilities of the job, education, experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities, as well as internal equity, alignment with market data, applicable bargaining agreement (if any), or other law.
